From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <d.afonchenko@dodopizza.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:13:49 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 113/115] Meridian: a document picture-in-picture window in its
 page's profile

A page in a space of another profile than the window's opened its
picture-in-picture window in the window's profile; the navigator then
dropped the source page as cross-profile and the CHECK in
PictureInPictureWindowManager::SetWindowParams took the browser down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
---
 chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
index 59803b3029..b67b03ac0a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/navigator/browser_navigator.cc
@@ -377,10 +377,14 @@ std::tuple<BrowserWindowInterface*, int> GetBrowserAndTabForDisposition(
             BrowserInitState::From(params.browser)->create_params().app_name;
       }
 
+      DCHECK(params.contents_to_insert);
+      // Meridian: in the profile of the page that opened it (a space's may not
+      // be the window's), so it stays that page's window.
+      profile = Profile::FromBrowserContext(
+          params.contents_to_insert->GetBrowserContext());
       auto browser_params =
           BrowserWindowCreateParams::CreateForPictureInPicture(
               app_name, params.trusted_source, profile, params.user_gesture);
-      DCHECK(params.contents_to_insert);
       auto pip_options =
           params.contents_to_insert->GetPictureInPictureOptions();
       if (!pip_options.has_value()) {
